  > Year-over-year, the unemployment rate for the combined territories remained unchanged at 5.8%. The Yukon's unemployment rate dropped slightly by 0.1 percentage points to 4.2%, while the NWT's rate fell by 0.8 percentage points to 5.0%. | Nunavut was the only territory to record an increase in its unemployment rate, up 2.0 percentage points to 10.3%, the highest rate in Canada. | Economic Conditions
